  "img": "systems/pf1/icons/skills/green_11.jpg",
  "name": "Beastmaster",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p><em>Beastmasters are warriors of the wilds that have forged close bonds with trusted animal companions. They focus their tactics on fighting alongside their companion animals as a formidable team of two. Though truly fearsome in battle, the beastmaster can be quite gentle when dealing with creatures of the wild. A beastmaster typically travels with one or more animal companions who show incredible loyalty to their humanoid friend.</em></p><p><em>Though a beastmaster prefers to spend time in the wild with his animal companion, he is not averse to venturing into civilized lands when the need arises. As long as animals may be found where he travels, the beastmaster will feel at home.</em></p><h2>Role</h2><p>The beastmaster's role goes far beyond merely wielding a weapon; it's about the symbiotic partnership with their animal companion. In combat, they operate as a formidable duo, the beastmaster often directing their loyal ally to flank enemies, absorb blows, or provide crucial crowd control, while they themselves contribute with their own martial prowess or ranged attacks.</p><p>Beyond the battlefield, the companion becomes an indispensable tool for exploration and survival, whether scouting ahead, tracking elusive prey, carrying gear, or providing an extra set of eyes and ears that extend the party's capabilities in the wild. This deep, almost instinctual bond allows for unique strategies and a playstyle centered on tactical cooperation, making the beastmaster a versatile asset adept at both augmenting the party's damage and providing invaluable utility, especially in outdoor environments. They aren't just a combatant; they're the embodiment of wild wisdom and loyal companionship, offering unique solutions to challenges both mundane and perilous.</p><h2>Class Skills</h2><p>The beastmaster's class skills are Acrobatics (Dex), Climb (Str), Craft (Int), Handle Animal (Cha), Heal (Wis), Intimidate (Cha), Knowledge (nature) (Int), Perception (Wis), Profession (Wis), Ride (Dex), Stealth (Dex), Survival (Wis), and Swim (Str).</p><h2>Weapon and Armor Proficiency</h2><p>A beastmaster is proficient with all simple and martial weapons, including whips and scorpion whips, as well as light and medium armor, but not with shields.</p><h2>Main Ability Score</h2><p>The beastmaster mainly focuses on Strength or Dexterity for martial combat, alongside Wisdom for their bond with nature and their animal companion.</p>",
      "instructions": ""
    },
